Might even beat you, Wylder.

255
00:13:03,908 --> 00:13:05,075
Yeah, I doubt that.

256
00:13:05,785 --> 00:13:07,661
I'm looking forward
to seeing you in the arena.

257
00:13:07,745 --> 00:13:11,081
If what Blake says is true, then I might
just have me some real competition.

258
00:13:12,666 --> 00:13:14,043
Enjoy the ride, Walter.

259
00:13:20,049 --> 00:13:21,717
When the county surveyed the fire damage,

260
00:13:21,801 --> 00:13:24,220
they discovered half the ranch
was improperly zoned,

261
00:13:24,303 --> 00:13:26,847
which could mean
no rebuilding of any kind.

262
00:13:26,931 --> 00:13:27,890
-Really?
-Yeah.

263
00:13:27,973 --> 00:13:30,643
But I sweet-talked our new friend
in the permits department,

264
00:13:30,726 --> 00:13:34,355
and he said if we get the rebuilding plans
into his office this weekend,

265
00:13:34,438 --> 00:13:35,898
he'll backdate and approve them.

266
00:13:38,317 --> 00:13:39,568
Okay.

267
00:13:39,652 --> 00:13:42,112
Will and I went over
the expansion plans, but…

268
00:13:44,406 --> 00:13:47,451
Look, I still don't know
that this is the right way to go.

269
00:13:47,535 --> 00:13:50,246
It just feels too soon
to be making a decision this big.

270
00:13:50,329 --> 00:13:52,623
We have to do it
before the offices open on Monday

271
00:13:52,706 --> 00:13:54,124
to avoid a zoning commission review.

272
00:13:54,208 --> 00:13:56,085
Richard's contact is doing us a solid here

273
00:13:56,168 --> 00:13:58,170
because once they open
that official review--

274
00:13:58,254 --> 00:14:00,339
We'll be stuck in red tape
for who knows how long.

275
00:14:02,883 --> 00:14:05,302
And there's one more thing.

276
00:14:06,762 --> 00:14:09,265
Because he's backdating the permits,

277
00:14:09,348 --> 00:14:12,726
we have to promise to break ground
on the barn by the end of the month.

278
00:14:12,810 --> 00:14:15,187
-At the end of this month?
-We can pull it together by then.

279
00:14:15,271 --> 00:14:16,814
It's not a big deal.

280
00:14:16,897 --> 00:14:19,525
Guys, these are huge changes.

281
00:14:19,608 --> 00:14:23,404
Like, we need more time to finesse them,
make sure they work for us.

282
00:14:23,487 --> 00:14:25,698
This is all just…
it's just moving way too fast.

283
00:14:25,781 --> 00:14:28,659
I need time to think about this,
and I gotta talk to Katherine.

284
00:14:28,742 --> 00:14:30,411
Okay. Um…

285
00:14:31,161 --> 00:14:32,288
-Let's take five.
-Yeah.

286
00:14:34,540 --> 00:14:38,752
Okay, look, I'm not gonna be forced
into making a quick decision on this

287
00:14:38,836 --> 00:14:40,671
because there's
a hang-up in the permits office.

288
00:14:40,754 --> 00:14:42,047
I'm gonna take as long as I need.

289
00:14:42,131 --> 00:14:45,342
We'll weigh our options before we
start tearing everything up out there.

290
00:14:58,147 --> 00:15:01,775
So I was thinking the paper
should interview some of the reps,

291
00:15:02,401 --> 00:15:05,696
maybe get the inside scoop on what
the colleges are really looking for?

292
00:15:05,779 --> 00:15:06,614
Thank you.

293
00:15:08,073 --> 00:15:10,159
Okay, I'm just talking to myself,
aren't I?

294
00:15:10,242 --> 00:15:11,160
Hmm?

295
00:15:12,161 --> 00:15:15,539
No, yeah, I love that idea.
Just repeat it one more time.

296
00:15:15,623 --> 00:15:18,542
I was saying the paper
can interview some of the reps maybe.

297
00:15:18,626 --> 00:15:20,711
Juniors and seniors
would really appreciate it…

298
00:15:20,794 --> 00:15:25,799
And here's Wylder Holt, three-time winner
of this event and a real rider to watch.

299
00:15:33,766 --> 00:15:36,644
Did somebody order
some cheap white wine in a plastic cup?

300
00:15:36,727 --> 00:15:39,563
Yes, this girl. Yes.

301
00:15:39,647 --> 00:15:40,481
Thank you.

302
00:15:41,106 --> 00:15:43,651
Thank you so much for coming.
I know it was last-minute.

303
00:15:44,360 --> 00:15:47,196
Honestly, I feel like I might've barfed
if I had to watch Alex by myself.

304
00:15:47,279 --> 00:15:50,366
No, it's okay. Honestly,
it was nice to get out of the house.

305
00:15:50,449 --> 00:15:51,659
How are things with Bob?

306
00:15:54,244 --> 00:15:57,998
But you will have to tell me
how this event works.

307
00:15:58,082 --> 00:16:00,042
Well, it's actually pretty simple.

308
00:16:00,125 --> 00:16:04,129
Um, when that gate opens,
a 2,000-pound, very angry bucking horse

309
00:16:04,213 --> 00:16:05,756
gets released into the arena

310
00:16:05,839 --> 00:16:08,842
and tries to hurl the rider off
while they hold on

311
00:16:09,677 --> 00:16:10,636
with one hand.

312
00:16:11,428 --> 00:16:14,098
Super fun especially for moms.

313
00:16:15,015 --> 00:16:17,601
Here's Wylder Holt,
three-time winner of this event

314
00:16:17,685 --> 00:16:19,395
and a real rider to watch.

315
00:16:20,562 --> 00:16:21,480
And he's out.

316
00:16:21,563 --> 00:16:25,359
Oh my, this guy is frosty as a snowman,
and it shows.

317
00:16:26,485 --> 00:16:28,862
Oh-ho! And there he goes!

318
00:16:30,698 --> 00:16:32,491
What a ride for Wylder.

319
00:16:32,574 --> 00:16:35,077
It's a full eight seconds for Wylder Holt.

320
00:16:35,160 --> 00:16:37,538
-Wow.
-And a near perfect ride.

321
00:16:38,080 --> 00:16:41,417
That's 83 points
for Wylder Holt, everybody.

322
00:16:41,500 --> 00:16:42,835
That's really good.

323
00:16:43,961 --> 00:16:46,005
-Is that good? Yeah.
-Yeah.

324
00:16:46,088 --> 00:16:47,756
-Kind of.
-So that's…

325
00:16:47,840 --> 00:16:49,591
Real competition for Alex.

326
00:16:50,467 --> 00:16:51,301
Oh.

327
00:16:51,802 --> 00:16:56,181
Put your hands together
for the one, the only, Wylder Holt!

328
00:16:58,267 --> 00:17:02,146
And on deck, we have Alex Walter
riding True North, round one.

329
00:17:02,229 --> 00:17:03,480
I competed here last week.

330
00:17:03,564 --> 00:17:06,442
The soil is packed pretty loose,
so be prepared for that.

331
00:17:06,525 --> 00:17:09,611
Remember to go with the horse,
even when you think you might be thrown.

332
00:17:10,696 --> 00:17:11,697
You'll be good.

333
00:17:14,199 --> 00:17:16,076
-And of course…
-I got this.

334
00:17:16,160 --> 00:17:19,038
…a big thank you
to the Rescue Rangers themselves.

335
00:17:19,121 --> 00:17:22,166
Put your hands together
for this year's pickup men.

336
00:17:22,249 --> 00:17:23,500
-I got us doubles.
-Oh.

337
00:17:24,752 --> 00:17:26,295
You're such a good friend.

338
00:17:27,296 --> 00:17:29,298
-Thank you. That's my girl.
-Okay.

339
00:17:29,381 --> 00:17:32,551
And now riding True North,
it's Alex Walter.

340
00:17:39,516 --> 00:17:41,393
The first appearance for young Walter

341
00:17:41,477 --> 00:17:43,145
in the Saddle Bronc Event,

342
00:17:43,228 --> 00:17:46,440
although he has had strong showings
in the Extreme Cowboy Event.

343
00:17:51,445 --> 00:17:52,279
-Okay.
-Okay.

344
00:17:57,451 --> 00:17:58,577
There he goes.

345
00:17:58,660 --> 00:18:02,289
True North is a tough horse. That horse
bucks like nothing else out here.

346
00:18:02,372 --> 00:18:03,916
Oh!

347
00:18:03,999 --> 00:18:06,335
And Walter's looking kind of shaky.

348
00:18:07,419 --> 00:18:08,587
-Oh.
-Oh God.

349
00:18:13,217 --> 00:18:14,593
And it's all over.

350
00:18:14,676 --> 00:18:17,513
Alex Walter not able to hang on here
in round number one.

351
00:18:17,596 --> 00:18:18,806
-He's okay.
-Yeah.

352
00:18:18,889 --> 00:18:21,183
-He's okay.
-He's gonna kill me.

353
00:18:22,267 --> 00:18:24,186
He'll be disappointed.

354
00:18:29,900 --> 00:18:31,777
I didn't realize you were so into rodeo.

355
00:18:33,153 --> 00:18:35,823
Yeah, well,
it's a big part of life around here,

356
00:18:35,906 --> 00:18:37,491
so it feels like I should be.

357
00:18:38,659 --> 00:18:42,162
How are you doing?
Feeling any better about Nathan?

358
00:18:42,246 --> 00:18:43,122
I'm fine.

359
00:18:46,875 --> 00:18:49,211
I forgot sugar. I'll be right back.

360
00:18:52,673 --> 00:18:54,800
Okay, what is going on?

361
00:18:57,136 --> 00:18:59,888
Me and Alex have been, you know…

362
00:18:59,972 --> 00:19:01,014
Oh, you're back together?

363
00:19:01,098 --> 00:19:02,975
No. I don't know.
It probably means nothing.

364
00:19:03,559 --> 00:19:05,269
Well, does it mean nothing to you?

365
00:19:05,352 --> 00:19:09,231
I don't know what it means, except that
I need to stay away from the rodeo today.

366
00:19:09,314 --> 00:19:12,693
Alex needs to be focused, and I would
never forgive myself if he got hurt.

367
00:19:13,944 --> 00:19:14,778
Okay.

368
00:19:14,862 --> 00:19:17,072
But what do you want to do right now?

369
00:19:17,156 --> 00:19:19,992
-I want to go to the rodeo.
-And what does Alex want you to do?

370
00:19:20,075 --> 00:19:21,702
He wants me to go to the rodeo.

371
00:19:21,785 --> 00:19:25,497
Right. So if you want to go to the rodeo,
and Alex wants you to go to the rodeo…

372
00:19:28,750 --> 00:19:29,626
Oh, hello.

373
00:19:31,128 --> 00:19:33,589
I was gone for like three seconds.

374
00:19:33,672 --> 00:19:35,841
Spill. What did I miss?

375
00:19:36,341 --> 00:19:40,637
How do you feel about hot cowboys
and all-you-can-eat snacks? My treat.

376
00:19:41,138 --> 00:19:42,222
I'm single now.

377
00:19:43,098 --> 00:19:45,142
Let's be real. You had me at hot cowboys.

378
00:19:45,225 --> 00:19:48,896
I have this cute top
I've been, like, dying to wear.

379
00:19:48,979 --> 00:19:50,022
Slay.

380
00:19:50,105 --> 00:19:51,565
-Should we go?
-Yeah.

381
00:19:58,780 --> 00:20:00,699
-What the hell was that?
-I know.

382
00:20:00,782 --> 00:20:03,035
I'm sorry.
I don't know what happened. Okay?

383
00:20:03,118 --> 00:20:04,828
I know True North is challenging,

384
00:20:04,912 --> 00:20:06,997
but you're making mistakes
you've never made before.

385
00:20:07,080 --> 00:20:10,250
-I think the cinches were coming loose.
-Is it because I'm here?

386
00:20:10,334 --> 00:20:12,252
I thought we were cool
with me staying your coach.

387
00:20:12,336 --> 00:20:13,170
That's not it.

388
00:20:13,253 --> 00:20:14,796
It's amazing that you're here.

389
00:20:14,880 --> 00:20:17,758
I… I'm sorry, okay?
I don't know what happened.

390
00:20:18,342 --> 00:20:20,344
You know horses can sense your mood.

391
00:20:20,427 --> 00:20:24,264
You still have one more round.
Do you trust yourself to be all in?

392
00:20:26,308 --> 00:20:27,142
Yeah.

393
00:20:27,976 --> 00:20:28,810
I do.

394
00:20:30,812 --> 00:20:31,813
Okay.

395
00:20:31,897 --> 00:20:34,775
Next out of the chute,
we have Tanner Jones, everybody.

396
00:20:36,276 --> 00:20:39,863
And there he goes, folks.
He's looking strong and steady!

397
00:20:39,947 --> 00:20:41,782
Look at that cowboy go, folks.

398
00:20:41,865 --> 00:20:45,452
We need to make sure
you're making noise as he goes around.

399
00:20:48,455 --> 00:20:49,748
No, I agree with you.

400
00:20:49,831 --> 00:20:52,709
If they're going too far too fast,
then we have to push back.

401
00:20:54,503 --> 00:20:56,004
Yeah, it's not what we wanted.

402
00:20:57,506 --> 00:21:00,217
Okay. We can talk about it more tonight.

403
00:21:00,300 --> 00:21:03,011
Bye. I'm sorry. That was George.

404
00:21:03,095 --> 00:21:05,472
-No problem. I remembered you were sweet.
-Yeah.

405
00:21:05,555 --> 00:21:06,598
Not salty.

406
00:21:12,896 --> 00:21:15,691
Um, so there's another round?

407
00:21:16,233 --> 00:21:18,568
Yeah, we get to do this all over again.

408
00:21:20,320 --> 00:21:21,822
I can't believe I agreed to this.

409
00:21:21,905 --> 00:21:23,949
The idea of another one
of my kids getting hurt.

410
00:21:24,032 --> 00:21:25,742
Another one? You mean Cole?

411
00:21:25,826 --> 00:21:27,703
That was two years ago.
That wasn't your fault.

412
00:21:27,786 --> 00:21:29,329
Yeah, but I let him go skiing.

413
00:21:30,539 --> 00:21:32,833
I mean, I can't help but think
even if I'd just said no

414
00:21:32,916 --> 00:21:35,919
or maybe if I'd gone with him,
the accident wouldn't have happened?

415
00:21:36,003 --> 00:21:38,505
Look, motherhood is 90% guilt and fear.

416
00:21:38,588 --> 00:21:40,132
Yeah. And laundry.

417
00:21:40,799 --> 00:21:42,050
I don't know how you do it.

418
00:21:42,134 --> 00:21:43,010
Do what?

419
00:21:43,093 --> 00:21:46,930
Well, just let them take chances
and make mistakes.

420
00:21:47,014 --> 00:21:49,016
Oh, believe me,
I don't always have a choice.

421
00:21:49,099 --> 00:21:52,269
Yeah, but I just wish
I was a little more like that with Grace.

422
00:21:53,645 --> 00:21:55,355
I just don't ever want to let her go.

423
00:21:56,606 --> 00:21:57,899
I get it.

424
00:21:57,983 --> 00:21:58,984
Oh.

425
00:21:59,067 --> 00:21:59,901
Here.

426
00:22:11,371 --> 00:22:13,999
Did you see the one that fell?
That poor kid.

427
00:22:14,082 --> 00:22:16,376
Blake likes to take risks
on the riders she coaches.

428
00:22:17,044 --> 00:22:19,629
That Alex guy turned out
to be a real waste of time.

429
00:22:20,130 --> 00:22:23,508
I bet the two seconds he stayed on
the bronc was a personal best for the kid.

430
00:22:23,592 --> 00:22:26,136
What about that Tanner Jones?

431
00:22:26,720 --> 00:22:29,139
Hey, Wylder, you might want
to watch your mouth.

432
00:22:29,222 --> 00:22:31,099
You're talking shit
next to somebody's brother.

433
00:22:31,183 --> 00:22:32,434
Hey, look, no offense.

434
00:22:32,517 --> 00:22:34,686
He's all right,
but if he keeps riding like that,

435
00:22:34,770 --> 00:22:36,438
he's gonna end up hurt or worse.

436
00:22:36,521 --> 00:22:38,065
Riding broncs ain't for everybody.

437
00:22:38,148 --> 00:22:41,151
He should stick to something
more his pace. No shame in it.

438
00:22:47,824 --> 00:22:51,203
Okay, assuming we break ground
in a couple weeks, we're gonna need…

439
00:22:51,286 --> 00:22:52,120
Yeah.

440
00:22:54,331 --> 00:22:55,415
George.

441
00:22:56,708 --> 00:23:00,087
You… you guys have to know
that this isn't what we agreed on.

442
00:23:01,004 --> 00:23:05,967
Right? The project was always
supposed to work alongside the ranch,

443
00:23:06,051 --> 00:23:07,886
and it's… it's completely taken over.

444
00:23:07,969 --> 00:23:10,180
Yes, this is more than we first discussed,

445
00:23:10,263 --> 00:23:13,475
but expanding means
that we can maximize our potential.

446
00:23:14,476 --> 00:23:15,394
Uh…

447
00:23:15,477 --> 00:23:17,979
And look, I've really thought about it,

448
00:23:18,063 --> 00:23:20,982
and I've thought about
how much this land means to our family,

449
00:23:21,066 --> 00:23:23,610
and I just don't think
that this is the right way to go.

450
00:23:24,444 --> 00:23:27,989
I'm… I'm sorry you feel that way, George,
but there's a lot at stake here.

451
00:23:28,073 --> 00:23:28,949
I understand.

452
00:23:29,032 --> 00:23:31,326
If we don't move forward immediately,
we could all lose out.

453
00:23:31,410 --> 00:23:33,245
I've already lost out, Richard.

454
00:23:33,328 --> 00:23:36,248
I lost the barn that my kids played in,
that I played in.

455
00:23:36,331 --> 00:23:37,499
My great-grandfather's shed

456
00:23:37,582 --> 00:23:40,752
no longer sits on the site
that he built it 100 years ago.

457
00:23:40,836 --> 00:23:44,548
And right now, I'm missing
my son's first bronc riding competition.

458
00:23:44,631 --> 00:23:45,465
I…

459
00:23:45,966 --> 00:23:48,176
I just… I don't…
I don't wanna lose anymore.

460
00:23:48,260 --> 00:23:51,388
Dad, we're gonna make sure
that doesn't happen.

461
00:23:51,471 --> 00:23:54,266
Will, this is my property,
and I have final say.

462
00:23:56,059 --> 00:23:58,562
I'm really sorry, but it stops here.

463
00:24:02,399 --> 00:24:04,860
George, I… I'm gonna be straight with you.

464
00:24:05,360 --> 00:24:07,112
I really want you on board.

465
00:24:08,488 --> 00:24:11,032
But if we can't agree on a way forward,

466
00:24:11,116 --> 00:24:14,494
the contract states that I have a right
to assume control of the project

467
00:24:14,578 --> 00:24:16,246
to ensure its financial well-being.

468
00:24:16,329 --> 00:24:17,205
It says what?

469
00:24:18,331 --> 00:24:19,166
Is that right?

470
00:24:19,249 --> 00:24:21,710
Yeah. There's a clause.

471
00:24:24,421 --> 00:24:29,259
You would cut us out of this project?
Make decisions about our land without us?

472
00:24:29,342 --> 00:24:31,178
Only if I had no choice.

473
00:24:34,389 --> 00:24:35,765
I'm sure that this contract

474
00:24:35,849 --> 00:24:38,560
probably also said this was originally
just supposed to be tents.

475
00:24:38,643 --> 00:24:40,353
It's probably not
as watertight as you think.

476
00:24:40,437 --> 00:24:42,105
George, I don't want it to come to that.

477
00:24:42,189 --> 00:24:44,608
-Then you shouldn't have threatened me.
-I'm not.

478
00:24:44,691 --> 00:24:49,613
Dad, we just have to figure out
a way to make this work, okay?

479
00:24:52,073 --> 00:24:53,700
I would like for you to leave.

480
00:25:01,500 --> 00:25:02,334
You know,

481
00:25:03,668 --> 00:25:05,629
I'm sure we can figure this out.

482
00:25:15,722 --> 00:25:16,806
Will?

483
00:25:27,526 --> 00:25:29,152
I'll call you later, Dad.

484
00:25:40,205 --> 00:25:41,122
Wow!

485
00:25:41,706 --> 00:25:42,958
What a view.

486
00:25:43,041 --> 00:25:44,000
I know.

487
00:25:44,793 --> 00:25:46,670
-They're so pretty.
-Do you know?

488
00:25:48,505 --> 00:25:51,508
-I'll be right back.
-Okay. Well, take your time.

489
00:25:51,591 --> 00:25:53,426
We'll just be here drinking in all the…

490
00:25:54,511 --> 00:25:58,139
Wait. Jackie, give me your jacket, please,
before my mom sees.

491
00:26:00,433 --> 00:26:01,268
Too late.

492
00:26:02,644 --> 00:26:05,313
It's okay.
Just, uh, go wish Alex good luck.

493
00:26:05,397 --> 00:26:07,816
I'll be here, quietly dying.

494
00:26:12,279 --> 00:26:13,738
-Hey.
-Hey.

495
00:26:14,656 --> 00:26:16,032
Thanks for coming out.

496
00:26:16,533 --> 00:26:18,034
Are you sure it's okay?

497
00:26:18,118 --> 00:26:20,161
I know you don't want any distractions,

498
00:26:20,245 --> 00:26:22,831
but I didn't wanna miss that moment

499
00:26:22,914 --> 00:26:25,083
when you ride that bronc
for the full eight seconds.

500
00:26:25,166 --> 00:26:26,126
Well,

501
00:26:26,793 --> 00:26:30,171
you obviously didn't see my first ride
or you would not be this confident.

502
00:26:30,672 --> 00:26:33,758
Actually, I did see it on the live stream.

503
00:26:34,634 --> 00:26:36,136
That's why I came.

504
00:26:37,012 --> 00:26:38,972
I just wanted to tell you that I…

505
00:26:39,848 --> 00:26:41,891
I know what a great rider you are.

506
00:26:42,517 --> 00:26:44,144
And I know you can do this.

507
00:26:45,604 --> 00:26:47,564
You just have to ride
like you know it too.

508
00:26:50,859 --> 00:26:53,612
Next up, Alex Walter in his second round.

509
00:26:55,030 --> 00:26:56,114
Uh…

510
00:26:58,408 --> 00:26:59,242
Wish me luck?

511
00:27:00,118 --> 00:27:02,621
You don't need luck.
You're gonna be great.

512
00:27:10,253 --> 00:27:11,630
Look. Look who's here.

513
00:27:12,339 --> 00:27:13,173
Hi.

514
00:27:13,256 --> 00:27:15,008
-Sorry.
-So good to see you.

515
00:27:15,091 --> 00:27:16,843
-How's it going?
-Okay.

516
00:27:16,926 --> 00:27:17,761
Hi.

517
00:27:21,806 --> 00:27:22,891
Hi.

518
00:27:25,769 --> 00:27:27,312
I didn't know Jackie was coming.

519
00:27:27,812 --> 00:27:28,647
Yeah.

520
00:27:29,564 --> 00:27:30,774
I'm glad she's here.

521
00:27:32,484 --> 00:27:33,318
It's okay.

522
00:27:33,818 --> 00:27:34,653
Yeah.

523
00:27:35,737 --> 00:27:39,157
We're back with Alex Walter
after a near wipeout in round one.

524
00:27:39,240 --> 00:27:41,451
Let's see if he can make up his points
here in round two.

525
00:27:43,370 --> 00:27:44,371
And he's out!

526
00:27:44,871 --> 00:27:46,831
He's looking strong, folks.

527
00:27:47,916 --> 00:27:50,043
Look at Alex Walter go!

528
00:27:50,126 --> 00:27:52,587
It's a brand-new rider, everybody.

529
00:27:52,671 --> 00:27:56,174
True North's giving it everything,
but Alex is holding strong!

530
00:27:56,257 --> 00:27:58,134
Whoa!

531
00:27:58,218 --> 00:28:02,180
That was something else, folks.
Let's hear it for Alex Walter!

532
00:28:03,431 --> 00:28:04,557
Whoo!

533
00:28:05,266 --> 00:28:08,561
And that's a score of 81 for Alex Walter!

534
00:28:13,525 --> 00:28:14,693
Yes!

535
00:28:17,028 --> 00:28:19,239
Okay, so we're gonna go see him.
Do you want to come?

536
00:28:19,322 --> 00:28:22,992
I'm gonna go and chat with Grace,
but you should be so proud.

537
00:28:23,076 --> 00:28:24,119
That was amazing.

538
00:28:24,202 --> 00:28:25,662
-Yeah.
-Thank you.

539
00:28:25,745 --> 00:28:26,746
Okay, bye.

540
00:28:26,830 --> 00:28:28,373
Okay, see you later.

541
00:28:28,456 --> 00:28:29,499
See ya. Bye.

542
00:28:32,168 --> 00:28:34,462
I gotta get back to picking up trash.

543
00:28:35,338 --> 00:28:37,215
Tell Alex congratulations.

544
00:28:37,298 --> 00:28:38,842
At least one Walter is a success.

545
00:28:38,925 --> 00:28:42,053
Okay, well, Alex isn't the only success
in our family. You know that.

546
00:28:42,137 --> 00:28:44,180
You won't say that
after you see my SAT scores.

547
00:28:44,264 --> 00:28:45,265
Cole.

548
00:28:45,348 --> 00:28:48,935
I studied for months,
and it still wasn't enough.

549
00:28:49,018 --> 00:28:50,228
You can take them again.

550
00:28:50,311 --> 00:28:51,855
Mom, without football

551
00:28:52,355 --> 00:28:55,650
or without a time machine
to go back and fix last year,

552
00:28:55,734 --> 00:28:59,070
I think college or…
or any type of real future

553
00:28:59,154 --> 00:29:01,072
is off the table for a while.

554
00:29:02,991 --> 00:29:04,033
No, you know what?

555
00:29:04,909 --> 00:29:05,910
I'll be fine.

556
00:29:05,994 --> 00:29:09,581
Just go tell Alex
how proud we all are of him.

557
00:29:11,875 --> 00:29:14,294
Cole, let me ask you something.

558
00:29:15,754 --> 00:29:17,672
Was I proud of the star quarterback Cole?

559
00:29:17,756 --> 00:29:18,882
Of course!

560
00:29:18,965 --> 00:29:22,469
You were always a natural athlete,
and football came easily to you.

561
00:29:24,512 --> 00:29:27,849
But the guy that's standing here now,
creating his life from scratch

562
00:29:27,932 --> 00:29:28,850
with hard work,

563
00:29:28,933 --> 00:29:30,894
after everything he's been through,

564
00:29:32,395 --> 00:29:34,397
I'm so much more proud of that Cole.

565
00:29:39,944 --> 00:29:42,280
You're gonna want
to give me a hug, aren't you?

566
00:29:43,323 --> 00:29:45,700
I think this is more embarrassing
than trash duty now.

567
00:29:45,784 --> 00:29:46,868
Listen to me.

568
00:29:47,368 --> 00:29:50,663
No matter what direction your life takes,
no matter what you end up doing,

569
00:29:50,747 --> 00:29:55,043
your father and I couldn't be more proud
or more grateful that you are our son.

570
00:29:56,795 --> 00:29:57,629
Okay?

571
00:29:59,923 --> 00:30:00,965
-Okay?
-Okay.

572
00:30:01,049 --> 00:30:03,176
-Okay.
-Okay. Okay.

573
00:30:03,259 --> 00:30:04,385
I love this face.

574
00:30:06,679 --> 00:30:08,765
Okay, go on before I hug you again.

575
00:30:14,854 --> 00:30:15,939
And now,

576
00:30:16,022 --> 00:30:20,318
for the Saddle Bronc Riding Division
of the 12 riders in the competition,

577
00:30:20,401 --> 00:30:21,820
these are your top five.

578
00:30:21,903 --> 00:30:25,365
Starting with number five,
it's Alex Walter!

579
00:30:25,448 --> 00:30:27,033
Whoo!

580
00:30:35,416 --> 00:30:36,668
Great job, Alex!

581
00:30:40,672 --> 00:30:42,173
Not too bad!

582
00:30:43,132 --> 00:30:44,551
And in first place,

583
00:30:44,634 --> 00:30:47,512
for the fourth time
at the Dubeau Valley Rodeo,

584
00:30:47,595 --> 00:30:53,560
with a hugely impressive score,
it's your champion, Wylder Holt!

585
00:31:08,575 --> 00:31:11,619
Girl, I can't take my eyes off you

586
00:31:11,703 --> 00:31:13,371
Yeah, we're learning to love

587
00:31:13,454 --> 00:31:14,956
About everything we messed up…

588
00:31:15,665 --> 00:31:17,709
Congratulations, Wylder.

589
00:31:17,792 --> 00:31:18,626
Thanks.

590
00:31:19,252 --> 00:31:20,795
That second round was a good ride.

591
00:31:21,296 --> 00:31:23,631
You pulled it back out there.
That's not an easy thing to do.

592
00:31:24,924 --> 00:31:26,634
Blake could be right about you.

593
00:31:27,343 --> 00:31:29,137
Maybe I do have to watch my back.

594
00:31:30,054 --> 00:31:31,723
I'll see you around, Alex Walter.

595
00:31:32,932 --> 00:31:34,642
Yeah, see you.

596
00:31:38,521 --> 00:31:41,858
Fifth out of 12,
that's a very strong debut.

597
00:31:41,941 --> 00:31:43,151
How does it feel?

598
00:31:45,612 --> 00:31:47,447
It feels like I won.

599
00:31:48,573 --> 00:31:50,199
I couldn't have done
any of it without you.

600
00:31:50,283 --> 00:31:51,868
Oh, I'm well aware of that.

601
00:31:53,536 --> 00:31:56,080
You know, my dad asked about you today.

602
00:31:56,164 --> 00:31:58,583
Okay, what does that mean?

603
00:31:58,666 --> 00:32:00,376
My dad sponsors riders
all over the country.

604
00:32:00,460 --> 00:32:03,212
So if he thinks you're good,
then you might have a future in this.

605
00:32:03,296 --> 00:32:06,090
-Really?
-He's holding tryouts in a few weeks.

606
00:32:06,174 --> 00:32:08,593
If you're interested,
he's looking for some new riders

607
00:32:08,676 --> 00:32:09,969
to compete under his banner.

608
00:32:10,053 --> 00:32:11,679
Wow, that's amazing.

609
00:32:11,763 --> 00:32:13,264
Yeah, but he's very selective.

610
00:32:13,348 --> 00:32:16,726
We'll need to put some work in,
but if you want to, then you could try.

611
00:32:16,809 --> 00:32:18,186
Yeah! Yeah, I want to.

612
00:32:18,269 --> 00:32:20,772
Okay, good. We'll work on that then.

613
00:32:27,946 --> 00:32:28,947
I gotta go,

614
00:32:29,530 --> 00:32:32,283
but I will text you about practice.

615
00:32:33,201 --> 00:32:34,827
Monday 5:00 a.m.

616
00:32:34,911 --> 00:32:36,454
-Blake.
-Yeah.

617
00:32:36,955 --> 00:32:37,830
Seriously.

618
00:32:39,415 --> 00:32:42,001
Thank you… for everything.

619
00:32:43,753 --> 00:32:44,587
Anytime.

620
00:32:49,217 --> 00:32:53,763
When you're right next to me

621
00:32:54,889 --> 00:32:59,060
I wanna hold you close
Till this old bar closes…

622
00:32:59,143 --> 00:33:01,104
Hey! Oh.

623
00:33:01,187 --> 00:33:04,148
-Hey.
-Hi. I've been looking for you.

624
00:33:05,149 --> 00:33:06,025
Nice top.

625
00:33:06,901 --> 00:33:09,946
Yeah, um, I know.
I'm sorry. I'll get rid of it.

626
00:33:10,697 --> 00:33:11,531
I…

627
00:33:12,991 --> 00:33:14,617
I think you look beautiful.

628
00:33:16,369 --> 00:33:17,370
But?

629
00:33:18,329 --> 00:33:19,205
But nothing.

630
00:33:21,249 --> 00:33:25,253
I think it's about time that I let you
make more of your own choices,

631
00:33:25,837 --> 00:33:27,547
whether I like them or not.

632
00:33:29,340 --> 00:33:31,676
But you might want to put on a sweater
before you come home.

633
00:33:31,759 --> 00:33:33,302
We don't want to upset your father,

634
00:33:33,386 --> 00:33:38,016
and I am not sure
that he is ready for this Grace just yet.

635
00:33:40,935 --> 00:33:42,061
I love you.

636
00:33:42,895 --> 00:33:43,813
I love you too.

637
00:33:47,984 --> 00:33:50,403
Change my shirt and check my phone

638
00:33:50,486 --> 00:33:52,947
Drive out where the sun goes down

639
00:33:53,031 --> 00:33:55,283
My darling, can I tell you

640
00:33:55,366 --> 00:33:58,870
That I can't stop this feel
Can't doubt what's real

641
00:33:58,953 --> 00:34:00,997
You've made
My little old heart stand still

642
00:34:03,374 --> 00:34:06,669
Oh my. Oh my.

643
00:34:06,753 --> 00:34:11,382
Dude, I swear, I just cannot pick up
one more hot dog bun without getting high.

644
00:34:14,635 --> 00:34:16,554
I mean, these people are animals.

645
00:34:17,180 --> 00:34:19,307
The trash can is right there.

646
00:34:19,390 --> 00:34:20,933
-What are we doing?
-Jesus.

647
00:34:23,436 --> 00:34:24,437
Oh.

648
00:34:25,938 --> 00:34:26,939
Hmm.

649
00:34:27,774 --> 00:34:29,650
Forgetting this entire day

650
00:34:29,734 --> 00:34:32,612
would… be, uh…

651
00:34:33,780 --> 00:34:34,906
Well,

652
00:34:34,989 --> 00:34:38,534
you have the power
in your hands, young Jedi.

653
00:34:41,871 --> 00:34:44,457
We text all night
Till the break of dawn

654
00:34:44,540 --> 00:34:45,833
Counting down those days…

655
00:34:45,917 --> 00:34:46,751
I'm good.

656
00:34:48,795 --> 00:34:49,712
It's all you.

657
00:34:49,796 --> 00:34:51,923
I can't stop this feel
Can't stop what's real…

658
00:34:52,006 --> 00:34:52,924
Okay, then.

659
00:34:54,717 --> 00:34:57,386
Just, uh… don't get so high

660
00:34:57,470 --> 00:35:01,307
these hot dog buns we've been picking up
start looking like snacks. Yeah?

661
00:35:02,683 --> 00:35:05,978
Yeah, I, uh… I make no promises.

662
00:35:07,688 --> 00:35:08,523
Okay.

663
00:35:19,367 --> 00:35:21,202
-Oh, hey.
-Oh, hey.

664
00:35:21,285 --> 00:35:22,995
-Can I have an autograph?
-Stop.

665
00:35:23,079 --> 00:35:26,207
Now that you're a big rodeo star,
I wasn't sure what was less embarrassing,

666
00:35:26,290 --> 00:35:27,333
that or a hug.

667
00:35:27,416 --> 00:35:30,878
Um, Mom, I placed fifth.
It's not like I won.

668
00:35:31,379 --> 00:35:32,463
It is to me,

669
00:35:33,214 --> 00:35:36,050
but I'm never gonna get used to
seeing you thrown off a horse like that.

670
00:35:36,134 --> 00:35:38,136
Well, uh, sorry

671
00:35:38,219 --> 00:35:41,139
because Blake thinks
her dad might wanna sponsor me,

672
00:35:41,222 --> 00:35:44,308
and if so, I'll be competing a lot more.

673
00:35:44,392 --> 00:35:46,644
So that means I have to…

674
00:35:47,145 --> 00:35:50,106
Watch me get thrown off a horse again?

675
00:35:50,189 --> 00:35:52,275
-Yeah.
-But not that horse, right?

676
00:35:52,358 --> 00:35:53,860
-That horse was horrifying.
-God, no.

677
00:35:53,943 --> 00:35:55,403
-Like from the apocalypse.
-Yeah.

678
00:35:55,486 --> 00:35:57,363
-Terrifying.
-Yeah.

679
00:35:59,615 --> 00:36:01,325
You looked really good out there, bud.

680
00:36:03,119 --> 00:36:04,871
I mean, I'm terrified for me, but…

681
00:36:06,289 --> 00:36:08,332
I am so happy for you
that you found your passion.

682
00:36:09,542 --> 00:36:10,543
It shows.

683
00:36:12,628 --> 00:36:14,714
Come here. Come here.

684
00:36:15,256 --> 00:36:16,257
Oh.

685
00:36:16,799 --> 00:36:18,593
-I love you.
-I love you too.

686
00:36:22,096 --> 00:36:24,140
-Thanks for coming.
-Anytime.

687
00:36:25,057 --> 00:36:26,100
What's going on?

688
00:36:27,643 --> 00:36:29,937
Richard threatened to cut me out
of the guest ranch project.

689
00:36:30,688 --> 00:36:32,773
How can I help you fix this?

690
00:36:34,025 --> 00:36:36,736
I found this vine,
out when I was looking for Murphy.

691
00:36:37,278 --> 00:36:40,114
And it turns out,
we used to have a vineyard out there,

692
00:36:40,198 --> 00:36:42,533
and a pretty damn good one
from what I read.

693
00:36:44,285 --> 00:36:45,578
Okay, so what's the plan?

694
00:36:45,661 --> 00:36:48,539
You still play golf with Victoria Chase
from Little Cap Winery?

695
00:36:48,623 --> 00:36:49,749
Yeah.

696
00:36:49,832 --> 00:36:51,375
I'd love to sit down with her.

697
00:36:52,543 --> 00:36:53,794
I'll set it up.

698
00:36:54,712 --> 00:36:55,755
Thank you, buddy.

699
00:36:57,048 --> 00:36:58,549
Thanks for coming.

700
00:36:58,633 --> 00:37:00,468
Those donuts were slammin'.

701
00:37:00,551 --> 00:37:01,677
They were!

702
00:37:02,929 --> 00:37:05,723
-This was great. I needed this.
-It was!

703
00:37:08,309 --> 00:37:10,228
We'll see you at the car.

704
00:37:13,147 --> 00:37:14,190
Did you see Alex?

705
00:37:14,273 --> 00:37:17,026
I was so worried when he fell,
but then he got right back up.

706
00:37:17,610 --> 00:37:20,529
Well, that's how we do it, right?

707
00:37:21,030 --> 00:37:24,116
We just keep falling and getting back up.

708
00:37:25,368 --> 00:37:27,286
Are we still talking about the rodeo?

709
00:37:29,163 --> 00:37:30,998
I got my SAT scores back today.

710
00:37:31,582 --> 00:37:32,708
And?

711
00:37:34,126 --> 00:37:37,546
Well, you know, not every college
relies on SAT scores anymore.

712
00:37:37,630 --> 00:37:40,967
Yeah, but my GPA has
basically tanked from last year.

713
00:37:41,050 --> 00:37:42,426
Did summer school help?

714
00:37:42,510 --> 00:37:43,678
Not enough.

715
00:37:44,303 --> 00:37:45,429
What if I help?

716
00:37:47,181 --> 00:37:51,185
This is what I'm good at.
I can make a study planner

717
00:37:51,269 --> 00:37:52,603
for the SAT retakes,

718
00:37:52,687 --> 00:37:55,731
and we can fill out applications together.

719
00:37:55,815 --> 00:37:58,109
We'll get you into college. I promise.

720
00:37:58,693 --> 00:38:00,069
Can't wait to get rid of me, huh?

721
00:38:00,152 --> 00:38:02,822
No, of course not. I… I just…

722
00:38:04,615 --> 00:38:06,534
I just want you to be happy.

723
00:38:09,161 --> 00:38:09,996
I know.

724
00:38:11,539 --> 00:38:12,456
Thank you.

725
00:38:12,540 --> 00:38:15,501
Welcome to
the Jackie Howard College Bootcamp.

726
00:38:16,085 --> 00:38:20,006
Um, Jackie, one… one more thing. Um…

727
00:38:20,089 --> 00:38:22,091
Can we not tell anyone about this?

728
00:38:22,675 --> 00:38:24,927
It's just I'm tired of being a failure,

729
00:38:25,011 --> 00:38:27,763
of… of needing people
to step in all the time.

730
00:38:27,847 --> 00:38:30,516
Can we keep it just between us?

731
00:38:35,980 --> 00:38:37,148
Of course we can.

732
00:38:38,858 --> 00:38:39,775
Just us.

733
00:38:58,669 --> 00:39:01,047
-Hi.
-Hey.

734
00:39:01,130 --> 00:39:04,550
I haven't been in here
since Cole let you move in.

735
00:39:05,092 --> 00:39:05,968
Yeah, I know.

736
00:39:06,052 --> 00:39:09,430
It's been really solid of him
to share his space with me like this.

737
00:39:10,556 --> 00:39:11,974
I should thank him more.

738
00:39:13,434 --> 00:39:15,019
Well, him and you.

739
00:39:15,102 --> 00:39:16,312
Why me?

740
00:39:16,395 --> 00:39:17,396
Because.

741
00:39:18,147 --> 00:39:20,775
I wouldn't have been able to ride
that well if you hadn't been there.

742
00:39:21,525 --> 00:39:23,277
I don't think that's true.

743
00:39:23,361 --> 00:39:27,073
I just told you to trust yourself.
You would've been great anyway.

744
00:39:28,240 --> 00:39:31,577
But being there, watching you ride,

745
00:39:32,453 --> 00:39:34,538
watching you do something you love…

746
00:39:36,082 --> 00:39:37,333
It was amazing,

747
00:39:38,084 --> 00:39:39,418
and it made me happy.

748
00:39:39,502 --> 00:39:41,462
You make me happy.

749
00:39:44,298 --> 00:39:46,509
We said we wouldn't do that again.

750
00:39:46,592 --> 00:39:49,053
Yeah, we did.

751
00:39:49,804 --> 00:39:53,599
You know,
we keep trying not to be together,

752
00:39:53,682 --> 00:39:56,227
and I'm not really sure I know why.

753
00:39:57,061 --> 00:39:58,521
You do know why.

754
00:39:58,604 --> 00:40:00,856
It's complicated.

755
00:40:00,940 --> 00:40:02,024
Not for me.

756
00:40:03,943 --> 00:40:08,155
Look, I know I said I needed time before,

757
00:40:08,989 --> 00:40:10,741
but to be honest, I was miserable.

758
00:40:11,492 --> 00:40:12,535
And now I'm not.

759
00:40:13,285 --> 00:40:15,162
I want to be with you, Jackie.

